course: dictionary
lesson: 6431
title: Mysterious and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mysterious means strange and hard to explain or understand. Read the words around it for clues. «The passage is long, gloomy, and, to tell the truth, decidedly shabby», and other tunnels branch off from a central hall, «mysterious and without apparent end». The place is spooky, and you cannot tell where it leads.
explain: A mysterious person keeps secrets or does not tell much about themselves. «Jacob wrestled all night with a mysterious man» tells you the man was strange and unknown, not just tall or quiet. Authors use this word to make you ask questions and keep reading.
explain: Mysterious can also describe something not yet explained. In science, a mysterious result may become clear later, after experiments. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: if «strange and hard to explain» still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Mysterious means strange and hard to explain or understand.
fact: A mysterious person keeps secrets or does not tell much about themselves.
fact: The adverb is mysteriously, meaning in a strange way that is hard to explain.
fact: Authors use mysterious noises, strangers and letters to build suspense and make the reader want to find out more.
fact: In science, something mysterious may be explained later by experiments.
exercise: «The noises in the attic were mysterious, and nobody could explain them.» What does mysterious mean here? | Easy to see | Loud and cheerful | Very wet | *Strange and hard to explain
exercise: Jacob wrestled all night with a mysterious man. What does mysterious tell you about the man? | He was very happy to meet Jacob | He was a famous king with a big crown | He was a loud and cheerful singer | *He was strange and unknown, and kept himself secret
exercise: Which would make a reader most want to find out more? | A list of shopping for Tuesday | A sunny day at the beach | A boring bus timetable | *A mysterious letter with no name on it
test: «The passage was mysterious and without apparent end.» What does mysterious mean? | Full of sweets and treats | Bright and cheerful | *Strange and hard to understand | Very short and narrow
test: Which sentence shows a person who keeps secrets? | He ran the race in ten seconds. | She laughed loudly with all her friends. | They ate lunch together. | *She never told anyone where she went after school.
exam: The lights went out mysteriously. What does mysteriously mean? | *In a strange way that is hard to explain | In a way that is easy to see | In a loud and happy way | In a slow and sleepy way
